# sources/manifest — code this fork owns outright, and where it goes in the checkout.
#
# `patches/README.md` is explicit that a file we add is not a patch, so these are copied into
# chromium/src by `./scripts/redrob.py apply` rather than diffed. They are also excluded from
# `export`'s "untracked files, move them into this repo" report, because they already are in it.
#
# Every path under sources/ mirrors its destination, so the mapping is checkable by eye.
#
# Format: SOURCE  TARGET

# chrome://redrob, the AI surface. See docs/AI_SURFACE.md. The only Chromium files this needs are the
# two one-line registrations in patches/, which is the whole point of putting the product in a WebUI.
sources/chrome/browser/ui/webui/redrob/BUILD.gn      chrome/browser/ui/webui/redrob/BUILD.gn
sources/chrome/browser/ui/webui/redrob/redrob_ui.h   chrome/browser/ui/webui/redrob/redrob_ui.h
sources/chrome/browser/ui/webui/redrob/redrob_ui.cc  chrome/browser/ui/webui/redrob/redrob_ui.cc

# Deliberately NOT installed yet, and this is the note that says so rather than leaving two files in
# sources/ that nothing copies and nothing references:
#
#   redrob.mojom       the browser <-> page interface docs/AI_SURFACE.md specifies. Wiring it means a
#                      mojom("mojo_bindings") target in the BUILD.gn above, the interface in
#                      chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders_webui.cc, and
#                      WebUIController::BindInterface on RedrobUI. Three more registration patches.
#   task_host_impl.h   the browser-side implementation of that interface, which also owns the sidecar
#                      handle. It cannot compile before the bindings exist.
#
# The page is a served, rendering scaffold without them. Add both rows here in the same commit that
# adds the bindings target -- a source file installed before the target that builds it is a broken tree.
